            <ArticleTitle>Acupuncture combined with spinal tui na for treatment of primary dysmenorrhea in 30 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To observe the therapeutic effects in acupunture treatment of primary dysmenorrhea combined with spinal Tui Na, and study its mechanism.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Thirty cases of the treatment group were treated by acupuncture combined with spinal Tui Na, and thirty cases in the control group were treated by routine acupuncture.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The total effective rate was 93.3% in the treatment group, and 73.3% in the control group, with a significant difference between the two groups (P &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Acupuncture combined with spinal Tui Na has good prospects for treatment of primary dysmenorrhea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
